[[!meta title="Why is Tails installing Thunderbird as Additional Software?"]]

Since Tails 7.5 (February 2026), Tails tries to automatically add *Thunderbird* to your
list of [[Additional Software|persistent_storage/additional_software]] to
improve its security.

Until Tails 7.5, a new version of *Thunderbird* was released by Mozilla only a
few days after we released a new version of Tails. As a consequence, the
version of *Thunderbird* in Tails was almost always outdated, with known
security vulnerabilities.

By adding *Thunderbird* to your list of Additional Software, the latest version
of *Thunderbird* is installed automatically from your Persistent Storage each
time you start Tails.

We also add to your list of Additional Software, the language package
corresponding to the language of your first session with Tails 7.5 or later. To
use *Thunderbird* in another language, see how to [[use *Thunderbird* in
another language|thunderbird#language]].

*Thunderbird* will no longer be included by default in Tails 7.N+x (MONTH YEAR)
and later.

# Successful migration

If the **Thunderbird Migration** dialog below appears when you start
*Thunderbird*, it means that Tails already added *Thunderbird* to your list of
Additional Software.

TODO:UX:Screenshot

# Manual migration

If the **Thunderbird Migration** notification below appears when you start
Tails, it means that Tails failed to add *Thunderbird* to your list of
Additional Software because the [[Additional
Software|persistent_storage/additional_software]] feature of your Persistent
Storage is turned off.

Select **Install as Additional Software** next time you start Tails to add
*Thunderbird* to your list of Additional Software.

TODO:UX:Screenshot

# Failed migration

If the **Thunderbird Migration** notificatio below appears when you start
Tails, it means that Tails failed to add *Thunderbird* to your list of
Additional Software for unknown reasons.

Please [[report an error]] to help us troubleshoot your problem.

